ide, water and carbon dioxide. (3 marks)</p>\n</div>","answerHtml":"<p>Original supplied handwritten marking key.</p><figure><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-additional/b414d47aba5ae6fa430f899a.webp\" alt=\"Supplied mole marking key question 5\" data-word-width-px=\"640\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" data-word-max-height=\"7\"></figure>","options":[],"optionsHtml":[],"correctAnswer":null,"markingMode":"manual","solutionOrigin":"supplied","sourceFile":"Test 3 2015.docx","sourcePath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/John XXIII/2015/Test 3 2015.docx","sourceBlobSHA":"6fc9cf32b79b89aa158ee3de6836b701d245facf","sourceSHA256":"595cd312fc0e689b2f8f3e38ebd0e04cd56d92d8bceb4df8d841ff0d208b860b","sourceKeyFile":"test 3 Mole answers.pdf","sourceKeyPath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/John XXIII/2015/test 3 Mole answers.pdf","sourceKeyBlobSHA":"fb249f7f50d71dc60078469b4e96b071c2363a78","sourceKeySHA256":"7336ad1f89e75933f4a646d45c0eb751cbb3b0edb2202b48d4983aca7f576910","sourceKeyNumber":5,"bankFile":"practice-studio-chemistry-john-mole2015.json","addedAt":"2026-11-07T00:21:00.500397Z","editableText":true,"questionFormat":"native-text","fontFamily":"Arial","fontSizePt":12,"responseLines":0,"sourceReviewNotes":[],"sourceTextFile":"Test 3 2015.docx","sourceQuestionOccurrence":1,"types":["Short answer"],"figures":0,"hash":"30171223a39a0e6d9dc3e17f4f6a3420f72d1aa21bab1b96b7d2361d768835f6"},{"id":"chemistry-additional-john-mole2015-written-6","subject":"Chemistry","year":11,"examYear":2015,"units":"1 & 2","number":6,"source":"Moles and Chemical Reactions (John XXIII, 2015)","section":"Short answer","marks":4,"topics":["Chemical calculations","Solutions and acids"],"subtopics":["Moles mass and composition","Stoichiometry limiting reagents and yield","Solutions solubility and concentration","Acids bases and indicators"],"mixed":true,"text":"(4 marks) A sample of copper (I) oxide was dissolved in sulfuric acid and the solution evaporated to dryness to yield 3.14 g of Cu2SO4. Cu2O + H2SO4 → Cu2SO4 (a) What was the mass of the copper (I) oxide sample? (4 marks) Use appropriate number of significant figures.","html":"<div><p><strong></strong> <strong>(4 marks)</strong></p>\n<p>A sample of copper (I) oxide was dissolved in sulfuric acid and the\nsolution evaporated to dryness to yield 3.14 g of\nCu<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>.</p>\n<p>Cu<sub>2</sub>O + H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub> →\nCu<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub></p>\n<p>(a) What was the mass of the copper (I) oxide sample? (4 marks)\n<strong>Use appropriate number of significant figures.</strong></p>\n</div>","answerHtml":"<p><strong>Teacher review required.</strong> Source wording/equation requires review: the printed copper(I) oxide equation omits water.</p><p>Original supplied handwritten marking key.</p><figure><img src=\"assets/chemistry/practice-import-additional/562ec6ea929f430bdd91cfd4.webp\" alt=\"Supplied mole marking key question 6\" data-word-width-px=\"640\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\" data-word-max-height=\"7\"></figure>","options":[],"optionsHtml":[],"correctAnswer":null,"markingMode":"manual","solutionOrigin":"supplied","sourceFile":"Test 3 2015.docx","sourcePath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/John XXIII/2015/Test 3 2015.docx","sourceBlobSHA":"6fc9cf32b79b89aa158ee3de6836b701d245facf","sourceSHA256":"595cd312fc0e689b2f8f3e38ebd0e04cd56d92d8bceb4df8d841ff0d208b860b","sourceKeyFile":"test 3 Mole answers.pdf","sourceKeyPath":"resources/ATAR/Chemistry/Assessments/11/John XXIII/2015/test 3 Mole answers.pdf","sourceKeyBlobSHA":"fb249f7f50d71dc60078469b4e96b071c2363a78","sourceKeySHA256":"7336ad1f89e75933f4a646d45c0eb751cbb3b0edb2202b48d4983aca7f576910","sourceKeyNumber":6,"bankFile":"practice-studio-chemistry-john-mole2015.json","addedAt":"2026-11-07T00:21:00.500397Z","editableText":true,"questionFormat":"native-text","fontFamily":"Arial","fontSizePt":12,"responseLines":0,"sourceReviewNotes":["Source wording/equation requires review: the 